        "source_evidence": {
          "unit_id": "L0003",
          "start": 79,
          "end": 636,
          "quote": "**Justification:** FDISCO (fluorescence-preserving DISCO) is selected for its exceptional ability to preserve endogenous fluorescence (e.g., GFP) while achieving high transparency in whole adult mouse brains. By utilizing pH-adjusted (pH 9.0) THF for dehydration and BABB-Df for clearing at a low temperature (4 ℃), it effectively maintains the structural integrity and signal intensity of fine neuronal processes like axons and dendrites, which is essential for 3D morphological mapping. DAPI is included to provide a reference for cell body distribution.\n",
